x86_64-linux  two recorded differences and neither is about the binding this case is for. clang copies the two-dimensional array member with a call to memset or memcpy where cxx1 writes the stores out - a compiler that ships no runtime has to, and value-init-empty-braces.nonames records the same thing - and clang emits only the C2 form of the inline constructor where cxx1 emits C1 as well, which implicit-move.nonames records. What the case checks, that `const double (&)[M][N]` binds to a `double[M][N]` lvalue without decay and that a shape or constness mismatch is refused, is checked by run.sh on every box.
x86_64-windows  the same memset difference: clang calls it to zero or copy the array member where cxx1 writes the stores out. Every other name agrees.
arm64-darwin  the same as x86_64-linux, the two Itanium targets emitting these the same way as each other.
